{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "Shared location rules for the four kits. `links` is the default place a LocationMessage opens when the host takes no `open`: `web` (Vue and the Flutter web/desktop target) by `provider` (osm when omitted), `apple` (SwiftUI, and Flutter on iOS and macOS) and `geo` (Compose, and Flutter on Android); `flutterTargets` maps Flutter's TargetPlatform to the column it uses (kIsWeb uses web). All three are null when a coordinate is not finite or out of range (latitude -90..90, longitude -180..180): the card then opens nothing. Coordinates are WGS-84 as stored in the message; Amap is told so (coordinate=wgs84). `coordinateFormat`: each number fixed to 6 decimals, then trailing zeros and a trailing point dropped, and a negative zero written 0. `titleEncoding`: the title is trimmed (blank = no title) and percent-encoded as UTF-8 bytes, every byte except A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~ written %XX in capitals (space is %20, never +). Without a title the Amap link has no name, the Apple link's q is the coordinate pair and the geo link has no parenthesised label. `label` is the coordinate line the picker and the card show when there is no map: each number fixed to 5 decimals (a negative zero written 0.00000), joined by \", \"; null for an invalid coordinate. `distance` is a POI row's distance: metres rounded half up below 1000, else kilometres fixed to 1 decimal; null for a missing, negative or non-finite value. `previewSize` is what LocationPicker passes to previewUrl: the map area's logical width and height times the screen scale clamped to 1..2, each rounded half up — device pixels on every platform (Compose converts dp with the density, never passes dp). Inputs avoid exact rounding ties so every platform's formatter agrees.",
  "coordinateFormat": {
    "decimals": 6,
    "trimTrailingZeros": true,
    "negativeZero": "0"
  },
  "titleEncoding": {
    "trim": true,
    "unreserved": "A-Za-z0-9-._~",
    "space": "%20",
    "hexCase": "upper"
  },
  "osmZoom": 17,
  "flutterTargets": {
    "android": "geo",
    "iOS": "apple",
    "macOS": "apple",
    "fuchsia": "web",
    "linux": "web",
    "windows": "web",
    "web": "web"
  },
